lesson: 219
title: Wheels on cycles
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: A unicycle has 1 wheel, a bicycle has 2 and a tricycle has 3: «uni» means one, «bi» two, «tri» three.
explain: Count the wheels of each kind on its own, then add them. Pedals are not wheels: every one of them has 2 pedals.
explain: 4 bicycles, 2 tricycles and 3 unicycles: 4 × 2 = 8, 2 × 3 = 6, 3 × 1 = 3, and 8 + 6 + 3 = 17 wheels.
vars: a=name b=2..12 t=2..6 u=2..5 z=2..9
answer: b * 2 + t * 3 + u
exercise: The bike shed has {b} bicycles, {t} tricycles and {u} unicycles. How many wheels are in the shed?
exercise: At the circus {u} clowns ride unicycles, {t} ride tricycles and {b} ride bicycles. How many wheels go round the ring?
exercise: A cycle shop sells {b} bicycles, {t} tricycles and {u} unicycles in one day. How many wheels has it sold?
exercise: {a} counts the cycles in the park: {b} bicycles, {t} tricycles and {u} unicycles. How many wheels does {a.he} count?
exercise: How many wheels are there on {t} tricycles, {b} bicycles and {u} unicycles?
exercise: {b} bikes, {t} trikes, {u} unicycles. wheels?
exercise: bike shed's packed — {b} bikes, {t} trikes n {u} unicycles from the circus club. how many wheels
exercise: {a} reckons a unicycle has 2 wheels lol. no. {u} unicycles, {b} bikes, {t} trikes, how many wheels
exercise: {b+1} bikes, no wait, {b} — one's at the shop — plus {t} trikes and {u} unicycles. wheels total
exercise: playground: {b} bikes n {t} tricycles n {u} unicycles, {z} scooters too but don't count those. wheels on the cycles?
exercise: How many wheels do {b} bicycles, {t} tricycles and {u} unicycles have, not counting any pedals?
test: Each of {u} unicycles, {b} bicycles and {t} tricycles gets a new tyre on every wheel. How many tyres are needed?
test: In the bike rack stand {t} tricycles, then {b} bicycles, then {u} unicycles. Find the number of wheels.
test: {a} oils every wheel of {b} bicycles, {u} unicycles and {t} tricycles. How many wheels does {a.he} oil?
test: A cycle parade has {b} bicycles, {t} tricycles, {u} unicycles and {z} people walking. How many wheels roll along?
test: trikes {t}, bikes {b}, unicycles {u}. how many wheels
test: pumped up every tyre on {b} bikes n {t} trikes, {u} unicycles too, knackered. how many tyres
test: There are {b} bicycles and {t} tricycles in the yard, with all their pedals, and {u} unicycles lean on the wall. How many wheels are there?
exam: A cycle store holds in stock {b} bicycles, {t} tricycles and {u} unicycles. Determine the aggregate number of wheels.
exam: Given that a procession comprises {b.words} bicycles, {t.words} tricycles and {u.words} unicycles, ascertain the total number of wheels in motion.
exam: Compute the number of tyres required for the complete re-tyring of {u} unicycles, {t} tricycles and {b} bicycles.
exam: Whereas a storage shed accommodates {t} tricycles, {u} unicycles and {b} bicycles, state the number of wheels contained therein.
exercise: The shed had {b+1} bicycles, but Grandad's old bike went to the tip when he passed away. Now the shed has {b} bicycles, {t} tricycles and {u} unicycles. How many wheels are in the shed?
exercise: some scumbag "borrowed" one of our bikes, it's never coming back. there was {b+1} bikes, plus {t} trikes n {u} unicycles. how many wheels we got now
test: The shop calls {z} of its bikes "pre-loved", which means second-hand but still for sale. Counting them too, it has {b} bicycles, {t} tricycles and {u} unicycles in stock. What is the total number of wheels in stock?
